        "original_id": "d9913aa6-6ff7-5584-b83f-c97007f5f5da",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Objects: NGC 166, PGC 2143\n- People: Francis Preserved Leavenworth, Frank Leavenworth\n- Places: Cetus, Mount Vernon, Indiana\n- Roles: American astronomer\n\nFacts:\n- Francis Preserved Leavenworth was born on September 3, 1858, in Mount Vernon, Indiana.\n- Francis Preserved Leavenworth, also known as Frank Leavenworth, was an American astronomer.\n- Francis Preserved Leavenworth died on November 12, 1928.\n- NGC 166, also known as PGC 2143, is a spiral galaxy in the constellation Cetus.\n- NGC 166 is about 2.6 million light-years away.\n- NGC 166 has an apparent magnitude of 15.18.",
